WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.620
Hey youtubers it’s charlie, welcome to my
forever evil edition of anime club.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.340
Last time I spent the whole video talking
about the best characters period and a lot

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.769
of evil made the list.

00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:12.900
So I thought it would be fun to dedicate an
episode to the best bad things.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.540
Who among us hasn’t rolled a sith warrior
in knights of the old republic.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.289
Playing evil is just more fun sometimes and
up until a certain point you didn’t see

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:19.289
a lot of evil characters celebrated the way
they are now.

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:21.130
Just to go outside the world of anime for
a second, Walter White has been the most popular

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.130
evil character in the past year.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.199
But the really awesome thing is that the best
evil characters never really see themselves

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:25.199
as evil.

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:28.470
The secret is that everyone even people in
real life are always the protagonist of their

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.470
own story.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.070
It’s just that sometimes when you zoom your
perspective out to include all the characters

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.540
on a show you find that the story isn’t
really being told from their perspective.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.470
Really quick though, congrats to my random
winners from my last anime club video.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.330
apropo of the wet snow you win the amazon
gift card and the milling, you get to pick

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:45.560
a future anime club topic.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.780
I’ll reach out to both of you on your channels.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.660
This week same prize.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.640
One random subscriber from the comments will
win a twenty dollar amazon giftcard and one

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.010
will get to pick a future topic.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.150
So let’s do this.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.850
I’m going to list my top 5 evil characters.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:01.739
and then give you guys a really good example
of a new anime series where the true protagonist

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:03.540
is evil.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:06.140
Everyone raise your glasses and let’s toast
“Gentlemen, To Evil”.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.499
By the way, the winner of this week’s gift
certificate will be the first person who can

00:01:09.499 --> 00:01:11.439
tell me which tv show that quote comes from.

00:01:11.439 --> 00:01:12.439
Here’s a hint, it’s the longest running
modern animated series in the world.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.439
Here’s a double hint, you can probably just
google the phrase.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:14.439
Let’s do this, number 5 - Griffith from
Beserk.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:19.049
He killed all his companions to become femto
the fifth member of the god hand and committed

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.380
some really really awful atrocities against
Guts.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.369
Before he was tortured for seducing the princess
you could say he was just a really selfish

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:29.829
person that eventually went insane.

00:01:29.829 --> 00:01:34.201
But because of his crimson behelit you could
also say there was a pre-destiny aspect to

00:01:34.201 --> 00:01:36.140
him becoming the true villain of the series.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.010
That’s the nature vs nurture argument that
all villains have in common.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:45.289
Are you a villain because it’s in your nature
or are you a villain because people turned

00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:46.679
you into one.

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:49.109
Number 4 - Johan Liebert from Monster.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:52.689
Guilty on all counts of Psychological crimes
against humanity.

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:58.920
The term villain is usually applied to big
monsters who physically attack other people.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.380
But sometimes psychological attacks are even
worse because it causes people to act out

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.729
on themselves.

00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:06.729
Johan twists minds indiscriminately.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:11.760
Not to be outdone by casual monsters he also
does outright murder people considered to

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.760
be his friends and family.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.760
Personally I think he’s worse for the mind
crimes he commits.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.660
I would say he’s like the Joker of the monster
series, but he actually has a grand plan.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.110
Where you could say the joker is just an agent
of chaos..

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.860
Now for the top 3, just a quick note.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.450
In order to make it into my top 3 I tried
to distinguish evil geniuses from characters

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.880
that are just plain awful.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:30.280
In order to be classified as such they need
to have a grand design, have all the best

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:36.120
monologues and a flair for the dramatic that
would make tom hiddleston as loki bow in submission.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.870
And so it goes Number 3 - The Major from Hellsing
Ultimate.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:44.120
All you need to do to understand him is watch
his war speech from episode 4.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.460
Not only does he have a grand design, he loves
revels in acts of atrocity.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:52.430
The fact that he’s a nazi makes it easier
to visually identify him as a villain, but

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:56.090
it’s really speeches like he makes that
sets him apart.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.470
Sub note for my top two.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:06.900
This is where evil geniuses begin to wield
the power of god and become much more ambiguous.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.490
The best evil characters don’t see themselves
as evil.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:10.490
Breaking Bad anime style.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.900
Number 2 - Father from Fullmetal alchemist
brotherhood.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.010
All that he wants is to know everything that
can be known and uses his nearly limitless

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.870
power to to achieve it.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:23.850
Because he’s immortal he becomes a kind
of hell on earth, unleashing the seven deadly

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:29.170
sins from himself, then killing those children,
so to speak, when it suits him.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:32.090
What’s worse, he takes the face of the hero.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:39.010
Even though edward and alphonse are the protagonists,
they’ll eventually look like hoenheim.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.530
Who’s face father took.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.240
He’s such a good character, that you cheer
for him a little bit when he almost achieves

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.240
his goal.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.420
Because what’s wrong with wanting to know
everything.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.340
And for my number 1 villain I had to select
a human.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.340
Because father is amazing, but he’s still
an ethereal create, like the living embodiment

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.340
of evil.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.340
And the only thing worse than that is a human
who becomes such as a result of his actions.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.670
This is like that walter white character.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:59.370
Someone trying to do good, weilding the power
of god, but ends up becoming the greatest

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.370
villain ever.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.230
So Number 1 is Light Yagami from Death Note.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.830
He tries to rid the world of evil and instead
becomes it.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:07.210
He’s so single minded in his quest that
he’d kill his own family if they tried to

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.210
stop him.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:10.040
Which becomes a really elegant contradiction.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.940
You try to protect your loved ones from evil
but kill them when they try to stop you from

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:16.940
becoming evil.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:22.100
It becomes this self fulfilling prophecy that
is common amongst all heroes that turn into

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.100
villains.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.630
So now it’s your turn to let me know who
your biggest anime villains are.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.840
and as I mentioned earlier, here are a few
recommendations for anime that’s new in

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.160
the last year where the main protagonist is
a villain.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.090
First is The devil is a part timer!

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.690
The premise is actually kind of funny.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.910
The devil is trapped in the body of a human
with none of his powers.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.620
So he has to get a job at a fast food restaurant
so he can live.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:45.180
And the hero gets a job as a telemarketer
to try and keep him in check.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:49.400
It’s just funny because it’s these epic
characters forced to do the most mundane things.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.420
It’s streaming for free on Funimation’s
website.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.650
Second is Flowers of Evil.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:59.250
The protagonist is a normal human student
who becomes really dark after getting humiliated

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.720
by his classmates.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.181
The animation is really different and the
pace is really slow.

00:05:03.181 --> 00:05:05.960
So it’s a lot different from Devil is a
part timer.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.760
It just depends on what type of anime you
favor.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.040
But it looks really interesting and it’s
streaming on crunchyroll.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.340
Feel free to make other recommendations for
anime with evil or just really ambiguous main

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.340
characters.

